That doesn't seem true; the function which causes the lightning bolt
(ghod_hitsu()) only causes a bolt of lightning. (This lightning bolt
actually doesn't even cause instant guaranteed death.)

You might be thinking of god_zaps_you(), which strikes you with a bolt
of lightning more directly; this is guaranteed death unless you are
shock resistant or reflecting (but it will not be reflected into any
specific direction, so it cannot kill other monsters).
If you survive that, the god will then use a wide-angle disintegration
beam on you that can be resisted by being disintegration resistant
(or by wearing an amulet of life saving; reflection does not work).
After that, they will summon some of their minions to fight you if you
were on the Astral Plane or in the Sanctum.

However, in this case ghod_hitsu() is called. god_zaps_you() is called
in angrygods() (which seems to be called in the case of god-angering
prayer), and if you attempt to convert a high altar (that is, in the
Sanctum or on the Astral Plane).


